<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Shamblers rise as a spread of xenotypes instead of only baseliners: vanilla Biotech xenotypes plus those of Big and Small,
		Alpha Genes, Det's, Rimsenal, VRE, Geist, Rim-Elves / Rim-Gnoblins, Merren and Biotech Expansion, each entry
		MayRequire'd on its mod. With Alpha Genes a few rarer ones join. With Cybranian - Anomaly Ghosts, its ghosts get a
		xenotype spread too (not installed here and its packageId is unknown, so that block keeps its mod-name check).
		Moved from Too Many Mods' core AA3B_ShamblerXenotype.xml (setting TMM_MoreShamblerXenotypes, default on); spaces
		after commas in a few MayRequire lists removed. The Alpha Genes block adds B&S / Biotech Expansion / Lamias xenotypes
		but is gated on Alpha Genes, as in the original.
		Removed 2026-10-13 (user): Big and Small's corrupted titan no longer rises as a shambler.
		Lowered 2026-11-08 (user): large races ten times rarer - Jotun line, Ogres, Lesser Oni, Abomination, Broodmother,
		Hive Queen, Tiamat, Nagaraj, Anacondaman 0.005 to 0.0005; Troll, Weaver, Devilspider, Glutton 0.02 to 0.002. Chances are
		absolute, so the difference goes to baseliners.
		Added 2026-11-08 (user): xenotypes from DanZinagri's Centaurs, Spider Xenotypes, Harpies, Catfolk, Lepthera and Muriden,
		sized the same way (large 0.0005, taur bodies 0.002, rarer variants 0.005, the rest 0.01).
		Checked with analysis/patch_sim.py: all apply against the installed mods; every xenotype name either exists or belongs
		to a mod that is not installed (Biotech Expansion, Det's Buzzers, Rim-Gnoblins, Merren).
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[@Name="ShamblerBase"]</xpath>
				<value>
					<xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
						<xenotypeChances>
